                            User account setup
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The built in Useraccount editor is supplied with several usefull commands.
When you want to enter the usereditor , you can do it offline or while a
user is online. To start the usereditor on an offline node, you need to
open the node screen, Press the EDITUSER icon or function key [F6].

You will be prompted:

NewUser or Account edit? 

You can select "N" for editing newuser accounts or "A" for normal account
maintance. A return alone will exit the usereditor.
Selecting "N" will start a newuser account scan. Users with accesslevel
defined under NEWUSERACCLEVEL otherwise default level 5, will be shown.
You can modify users account using presets or manually edit the account.
All functions are accessed through a single letter command. (A - Y).




* Presets
---------
Pre defined setup files for user accounts, are located in the PRESETS
directory in your system mainpath directory. the name are PRESET_1 ,where
1 is presetnumber, you can define 10 presets.
Preset 1 to 5 can be used both by sysop and cosysop, but preset 6-10
are only accessable by sysop.
Preset example below shows how to define a preset.

*=> PRESET setup example     (Filename: PRESET_1)
----------------------------------------------
CONFJOIN		AMIGA		;Conference to join at next login
ACCLEVEL		100		;Give user access 100
USERTYPE		SYSOP		;His usertype name
RATIO			0		;ratio given
RATIOTYPE		DISABLED	;ratio type
DLDAYLIMIT		999999999	;daily download byte limit.
TIMEDAYLIMIT		60		;Daily time limit for one day
CHATDAYLIMIT		15		;Multichat time limit, daily.
UPLOADFILES		0		;Upload files   to start with
DOWNLOADFILES		0		;download files -------------
UPLOADBYTES		0		;upload bytes   to start with
DOWNLOADBYTES		0               ;download bytes -------------
----------------------------------------------




* Account edit (old user)
If you want to edit an user account select "A" at the prompt when asked
for newuser/account edit.
You will then be prompted to enter username or usernumber.

Enter UserName/UserNumber: 1

*-> Account example , below is an example of an account displayed.
------------------------------------------------------------------
