* Help on function commands
---------------------------

A - Forward mail.
    If a user temporary is on vacation or do not want to receive the
    Messages sent to him, you can select another receiver as destination
    for messages addressed to this person.
    You will be prompted for a username or number.

B - Forward mail to date.
    Enter date user will return to the system, and be able to receive
    his mail.

C - Edit users name...

D - Edit USERTYPE type

E - Edit users Location

F - Edit international phone number code

G - Change users voice phone number

H - Change users data/fax number

I - Change users celluar/mobile number

J - Change users password
    This password is used when user is loggin on the system, and prompted
    for it, when user enters a name.

K - Password 2. Reserved for Future use.

L - Fido net password. Reserved for future use.

M - Change users timelimit on the system. value is in minutes.

N - Change users time used on the system this day.

O - Chat limit, users chat timelimit when in multichat.

P - Chat time used today.

(BELOW FUNCTIONS ARE ALL CONFERENCE RELATED INFORMATION IF YOU DID NOT
 CHOOSE TO WORK WITH SHARED CONFERENCE DATA INFORMATION)

Q - Change users accesslevel 

R - Change users upload bytes to the system. 

S - Change users download bytes to the system.

T - Change users upload files to the system.

U - Change users download files to the system.

V - Change users Ratiotype... where: 0 -> DISABLED , 1 -> BYTES, 2 -> FILES

W - Change users ratio

X - Change users download byte limit for a day.

Y - Change users download bytes today.



* Other functions in the editor
-------------------------------

You can move around in user accounts with "<" and ">"..

If you have different setups for each conference, with u/l & d/l ,ratio etc.
You can jump to a users other conference with the arrow keys, Left/Right.

To save a modified account press "~"

Press Control-C to edit the quick conference account editor.

Escape exits the editor.

You can view users answer to your "answer.scp", if you have used this.
Press the "|" letter and the answer will be displayed.

[DEL]  activates / deletes an user account.

[TAB] jumps to next available user account.




* Online Editing of user
------------------------

If you edit a user online you can press [F6] or ICON: EDITUSER.
This user editor is limited to edit only information for current user
and current conference data. If a user modifies his data while sysop
is in the editor, Editor will update all fields changed.

[TAB] key is the EXIT button or you can press the closewindow gadget.

NOTE: User will not notice you are editing the account, and he is still
able to continue using the system.

